From 24e1d0282675ab09563f33f40d41651526d2e8a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chengyi Zhao <zhaochengyi@uniontech.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:56:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] alsa-plugin: fix error check in update_active()

pw->error is negative (-EINVAL, -errno, or a negative PipeWire error),
but update_active() checks pw->error > 0, so the condition never matches.
A stream or core error calls update_active(&pw->io, false), so the eventfd
is left inactive and an application blocked in poll() may sleep forever.

1081b8f07 added force_wakeup for SETUP/XRUN/stop, but does not cover a
plain PipeWire error.  Check for a negative error instead.

--- a/pipewire-alsa/alsa-plugins/pcm_pipewire.c
+++ b/pipewire-alsa/alsa-plugins/pcm_pipewire.c
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 
 	avail = snd_pcm_ioplug_avail(io, pw->hw_ptr, io->appl_ptr);
 
-	if (pw->error > 0) {
+	if (pw->error < 0) {
 		active = true;
 	}
 	else if (io->state == SND_PCM_STATE_DRAINING) {
